## Available capture boundaries

Use the available captures to choose the narrowest exact observation claim.
{% if "assistant_message" in available_observation_kinds %}
- The `assistant_message` capture holds the full text of every assistant reply
  in the conversation. A reply-level claim about what a reply says — for
  example, that it discloses a supplied sensitive value, confirms an action,
  or states a fact — is observable when the supplied context gives a concrete
  criterion to check it against. Comparative or group-difference claims still
  require paired evidence.
- A precondition that sets up the situation is not an observation
  requirement. When supplied facts establish it (for example, that a subject
  has no approved source, or what the approved source says), a claim about
  what the reply states is observable through `assistant_message` even
  though returned results are not captured. Judge the reply against the
  supplied facts and the request, not against origin, authorship, or timing
  metadata that the reply does not carry.
{% endif %}
{% if "tool_call" in available_observation_kinds %}
- A complete `tool_call` capture holds the ordered sequence of tool calls the
  agent made in the conversation, with names and decoded arguments. It supports
  `command_attempt` claims that a call to an operation occurred, what its
  arguments were, the order of two calls within that same capture (not
  cross-channel ordering), and that no call to an operation occurred in the
  conversation (an omission). An omission is a `command_attempt` claim naming
  the operation that should have been called.
{% endif %}

Still unobservable under this contract:
- the contents of model-to-model prompts;
- internal component signals or filter stages;
{% if "snapshot" not in available_observation_kinds or "state_effect" in unsupported_observation_claims %}
- backend state effects without a snapshot;
{% endif %}
{% if "tool_result" not in available_observation_kinds or "returned_result" in unsupported_observation_claims %}
- returned results;
{% endif %}
- the absence of a reply;
- ordering against an event outside the captured conversation.

Do not substitute a nearby command attempt for an unsupported reply, returned
result, state effect, internal signal, missing-reply, or cross-channel-ordering
claim. If the available capture does not cover the exact claim, set
`observable: false` and explain the observation gap.
